---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { company, site } from '../data/site';
---

<Legal title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using VigilOps paid plans and this website.">
  <p>
    These terms apply to paid VigilOps plans and to vigilops.cloud. VigilOps is provided by {company.legalName}
    ("we", "us"), {company.address}, {company.country}. By buying a plan you agree to these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The open-source software</h2>
  <p>
    The VigilOps software is open source under the <a href={`${site.github}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT license</a>. Your use
    of the software itself is governed by that license, whether or not you have a paid plan. The software is provided "as
    is", without warranty of any kind.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Paid plans</h2>
  <p>Pro and Team plans give you, for as long as your subscription is active:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>support by email (and a shared chat on Team) with the response times listed on the pricing page, on business days;</li>
    <li>help for the number of servers listed for your plan;</li>
    <li>access to VigilOps Cloud features as they become available to your plan.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Features marked "coming soon" are not yet available. We aim to release them but do not promise a date. Response times
    are targets, not guarantees, unless a written agreement says otherwise.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Billing</h2>
  <p>
    Plans are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, through our payment provider Bachs, and renew automatically until you
    cancel. Prices are shown in US dollars and may exclude taxes. If we change the price of your plan we will email you
    at least 30 days before it applies; the founding price shown when you subscribed stays in place while your
    subscription remains active.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time. Your plan stays active until the end of the period already paid for. Refunds are covered
    by our <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You are responsible for your servers, your data and your backups, including testing that backups can be restored.</li>
    <li>You must not use VigilOps or our support to break the law or to access systems you are not authorised to access.</li>
    <li>Keep your Telegram bot tokens, API keys and storage credentials secret.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for lost data, lost profits or indirect damages, and our total
    liability for a paid plan is limited to the amount you paid us for it in the 12 months before the claim.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms and will email subscribers about material changes. These terms are governed by the laws of
    {company.country}. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${company.contactEmail}`}>{company.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
